            <ArticleTitle>[Structural changes in the gastric and duodenal mucosal capillaries in asthma].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>37-41</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Morphological examination of microcirculatory bed vessels in the gastric and duodenal mucous membranes was performed in asthmatic patients. The gastroduodenal area showed signs of capillary dysfunction and a vascular component of mucosal remodeling, like bronchial wall remodeling in asthma.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
